import{_ as a,o as t,c as r,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.BdWD-ld-.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-23","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-23"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-23.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-23.md","lastUpdated":null}'),o={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-23.md"};function i(s,e,d,c,l,p){return t(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence-·-2026-11-23" tabindex="-1">Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-23 <a class="header-anchor" href="#agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence-·-2026-11-23" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-23&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Core conclusion: enterprise employees need separate evidence for action approval, result publication, delivery acceptance and execution recovery. Several SDK governance proposals remain OPEN; Orca paired-agent activation is distinct from its undeployed cloud wake service.</p><p>33 fact observations and six analyses. Event times are UTC; report date Asia/Shanghai. New and backfilled observations retain actual dates; proposal updates are not releases. Zero new experiments/articles/formal reviews. A separate November 22 experiment and bilingual article were reconciled, not performed again today.</p><h2 id="cross-day-reconciliation" tabindex="-1">Cross-day reconciliation <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-day-reconciliation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cross-day reconciliation&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Source date + original ID</th><th>Actual disposition and scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2026-11-19 A1</td><td>Retain November 19 scoped skill-boundary results; not rerun, live mounting/authority/execution remain pending.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A2</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A3</td><td>Partially complete: separate November 22 study used three controls/six new Node processes for per-file read receipts and restart requeue. Simulated PM events prove requeue only; actual PM consumption, version binding and independent QA remain pending.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A4</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A5</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A6</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-19 A7</td><td>Pending: upstream/document checks only; original experiments not run.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-17 A2</td><td>Pending; retain historical stop regressions; external-effect/lost-receipt tests remain unrun.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-17 A4</td><td>Partially complete via the same November 22 study as 2026-11-19 A3; do not count twice.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-16 A1</td><td>Pending; real dual-host takeover unrun.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-16 A2</td><td>Pending; real Core/ACP trials unrun.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A1</td><td>Pending; retry authority/resource/budget experiments unrun.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A2</td><td>Partially complete via the shared per-file receipt study; independent acceptance/version binding remain pending.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A3</td><td>Pending; failed-governance-check and credential negative controls unrun.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A4</td><td>Document review advanced: Orca source MIT verified; product/isolation/hosted terms remain pending.</td></tr><tr><td>2026-11-22 A5</td><td>Pending; install/migration/recovery/event/upgrade trials unrun.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The November 22 study pinned CodeFlowMu Runtime 3.1.11 commit 794123058b8db012ca0da189b43fdf0c5ec2ff04. Zero/one/two read receipts led to two/one/zero requeued reports in fresh processes; failed reads produced no receipt. Six isolated processes used real Watcher/Dispatcher/Stores with simulated PM session events. This proves requeue only, not model consumption, version binding or acceptance. <a href="./../../research/2026-11-22-digital-employee-handoff-receipts">Experiment article</a></p><h2 id="fact-observations" tabindex="-1">Fact observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#fact-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Fact observations&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="o1-·-resume-built-in-codex-approvals-with-sdk-tool-hooks" tabindex="-1">O1 · Resume built-in Codex approvals with SDK tool hooks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-·-resume-built-in-codex-approvals-with-sdk-tool-hooks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 · Resume built-in Codex approvals with SDK tool hooks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/openai-agents-python · 2026-11-23T01:56:35Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: feat/simple-codex</p><p>Merged into experimental feat/simple-codex, not main or a stable release. Store the transformed action for review; a fresh worker does not transform approved input twice. Missing callbacks leave approval pending; output processing precedes storage/publication; workers need matching callbacks. Upstream Redis restart tests report one execution and no extra writes on denial/duplicate decisions; not rerun locally.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6155" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o2-·-feat-redact-runner-payloads-before-streaming-and-persistence" tabindex="-1">O2 · feat: redact Runner payloads before streaming and persistence <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-·-feat-redact-runner-payloads-before-streaming-and-persistence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 · feat: redact Runner payloads before streaming and persistence&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/openai-agents-python · 2026-11-23T01:56:29Z · <strong>OPEN</strong> · target: feat/simple-codex</p><p>OPEN against feat/simple-codex. Proposed redaction spans instructions, arguments, results and snapshots, withholding raw deltas and requiring the redactor on restore. RunState 1.24/checkpoint v2 require readers upgraded first. Tool inputs may change; provider/app logs, opaque media and old copies are excluded. Upstream figures are not local results.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6154" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o3-·-transform-selected-native-mcp-results-before-publication" tabindex="-1">O3 · Transform selected native MCP results before publication <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-·-transform-selected-native-mcp-results-before-publication" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 · Transform selected native MCP results before publication&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/openai-agents-python · 2026-11-22T22:36:19Z · <strong>OPEN</strong> · target: feat/simple-codex</p><p>OPEN experimental-branch proposal for whole-result transforms keyed by server/raw tool name, bounded to 1 MiB and preserving isError. Core rollout can record originals first, so detected recording settings refuse activation. Independent child threads and arbitrary logs are excluded; startup snapshots do not detect later identity/name changes.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6133" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o4-·-feat-tools-edit-selected-tool-results-before-tracing-and-publication" tabindex="-1">O4 · feat(tools): edit selected tool results before tracing and publication <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-·-feat-tools-edit-selected-tool-results-before-tracing-and-publication" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 · feat(tools): edit selected tool results before tracing and publication&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/openai-agents-python · 2026-11-22T22:41:19Z · <strong>OPEN</strong> · target: feat/simple-codex</p><p>OPEN experimental-branch proposal editing selected results before traces, history and the next model request. Exact tool/server object matching can reject restored pending calls missing editors before execution; old snapshots lack this requirement. Invalid edits block publication without undoing completed effects.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6141" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o5-·-feat-stream-approved-text-previews-and-notify-callers-of-accepted-output" tabindex="-1">O5 · feat: stream approved text previews and notify callers of accepted output <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-·-feat-stream-approved-text-previews-and-notify-callers-of-accepted-output" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 · feat: stream approved text previews and notify callers of accepted output&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/openai-agents-python · 2026-11-22T22:56:46Z · <strong>OPEN</strong> · target: feat/simple-codex</p><p>OPEN experimental-branch proposal. Drain raw streams privately and publish approved prefixes; notify final acceptance only after guardrails, persistence and cleanup, never on failed/interrupted runs. Previews cannot be retracted; final notifications contain no text and do not replace full-answer display policy.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6131" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o6-·-feat-let-agent-hooks-request-another-turn-before-accepting-a-final-answer" tabindex="-1">O6 · feat: let agent hooks request another turn before accepting a final answer <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-·-feat-let-agent-hooks-request-another-turn-before-accepting-a-final-answer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 · feat: let agent hooks request another turn before accepting a final answer&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/openai-agents-python · 2026-11-22T23:26:22Z · <strong>OPEN</strong> · target: feat/simple-codex</p><p>OPEN experimental-branch proposal: step_policy chooses finish/continue on proposed answers, with handoff precedence, turn limits and output guardrails retained; continuing skips end hooks. Earlier stream events and tool effects cannot be undone.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6124" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o7-·-feat-add-typed-decisions-and-specialist-handoffs" tabindex="-1">O7 · feat: add typed Decisions and specialist handoffs <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-·-feat-add-typed-decisions-and-specialist-handoffs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 · feat: add typed Decisions and specialist handoffs&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/openai-agents-python · 2026-11-22T23:06:23Z · <strong>OPEN</strong> · target: feat/simple-codex</p><p>OPEN experimental-branch proposal selecting currently permitted labels and rechecking target/authority before handoff; restoration needs fresh context_override. No automatic fallback/retry on failed selection; OpenAI adapter requires 2–255 labels and does not auto-transfer with one target.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6132" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o8-·-automatically-resume-disconnected-cloud-conversations-in-the-tui" tabindex="-1">O8 · Automatically resume disconnected cloud conversations in the TUI <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-·-automatically-resume-disconnected-cloud-conversations-in-the-tui" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 · Automatically resume disconnected cloud conversations in the TUI&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/codex · 2026-11-22T23:14:28Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Reattach when idle with no answers to restore; retain drafts/queues and verify paginated history completeness and overlap before accepting live events. Failed verification keeps sending paused.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63211" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o9-·-reuse-runtime-authenticated-responses-websockets" tabindex="-1">O9 · Reuse runtime-authenticated Responses WebSockets <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-·-reuse-runtime-authenticated-responses-websockets" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 · Reuse runtime-authenticated Responses WebSockets&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/codex · 2026-11-22T19:13:04Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Runtime-authenticated WebSocket reuse requires matching headers, connection key, runtime ID and parent affinity. Credential/account changes create new connections; paused runtimes are rejected on reconnect.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63175" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o10-·-fix-account-refresh-for-new-cloud-sessions" tabindex="-1">O10 · Fix account refresh for new cloud sessions <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-·-fix-account-refresh-for-new-cloud-sessions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 · Fix account refresh for new cloud sessions&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/codex · 2026-11-22T18:24:54Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Cloud account identity comes from the authenticated connection&#39;s account/read, avoiding unsupported config/read when model providers change.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63171" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o11-·-discard-tui-typeahead-after-prompt-rewind-and-fork" tabindex="-1">O11 · Discard TUI typeahead after prompt rewind and fork <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-·-discard-tui-typeahead-after-prompt-rewind-and-fork" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 · Discard TUI typeahead after prompt rewind and fork&quot;">​</a></h3><p>openai/codex · 2026-11-22T21:19:13Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Pause and drain typeahead before restoring rewound/forked prompts so buffered Enter cannot submit an unedited instruction. Focus/resize handling is included; this is intent integrity, not general authorization proof.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63193" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o12-·-honor-explicit-turn-continuation-in-chat-completions-and-responses" tabindex="-1">O12 · Honor explicit turn continuation in Chat Completions and Responses <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-·-honor-explicit-turn-continuation-in-chat-completions-and-responses" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 · Honor explicit turn continuation in Chat Completions and Responses&quot;">​</a></h3><p>OpenHands/software-agent-sdk · 2026-11-22T19:53:17Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Explicit end_turn:false continues after emitting a message in both APIs; streaming preserves the last explicit value. True/absent metadata retain behavior; unmarked premature endings remain outside scope. 114 tests are upstream.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/7067" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o13-·-clarify-when-agents-should-continue-authorized-work" tabindex="-1">O13 · Clarify when agents should continue authorized work <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-·-clarify-when-agents-should-continue-authorized-work" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 · Clarify when agents should continue authorized work&quot;">​</a></h3><p>OpenHands/software-agent-sdk · 2026-11-22T19:53:20Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Prompt encourages continuing authorized troubleshooting/verification/monitoring while retaining actual gates and limits. Prompt-only, with 118 upstream prompt tests and no live-model evaluation or dispatch/security change.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/7068" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o14-·-fix-projects-build-project-profiles-on-the-active-llm-when-the-user-s-names-none" tabindex="-1">O14 · fix(projects): build project profiles on the active LLM when the user&#39;s names none <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-·-fix-projects-build-project-profiles-on-the-active-llm-when-the-user-s-names-none" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 · fix(projects): build project profiles on the active LLM when the user&#39;s names none&quot;">​</a></h3><p>OpenHands/software-agent-sdk · 2026-11-22T14:02:42Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. New project roles fall back to the active LLM only for missing saved references; valid references stay and existing bad project profiles are not overwritten, requiring a manual save. Upstream live-server 34/34 results are not local testing.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/7056" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o15-·-fix-workspaces-let-the-full-disk-read-only-save-inventory-a-large-workspace" tabindex="-1">O15 · fix(workspaces): let the full-disk read-only save inventory a large workspace <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-·-fix-workspaces-let-the-full-disk-read-only-save-inventory-a-large-workspace" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 · fix(workspaces): let the full-disk read-only save inventory a large workspace&quot;">​</a></h3><p>paperclipai/paperclip · 2026-11-22T17:47:27Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: master</p><p>Merged master. Raise read-only recovery inventory scanning from 100,000 to two million entries to align with the 64 MiB manifest capacity, retaining source safety/timeouts/deadlines. Upstream 101,202-entry tests do not establish arbitrary-size recovery.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22546" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o16-·-fix-network-evaluate-turn-within-expectations-on-workflow-and-discussion-channels" tabindex="-1">O16 · fix(network): evaluate turn_within expectations on workflow and discussion channels <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-·-fix-network-evaluate-turn-within-expectations-on-workflow-and-discussion-channels" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 · fix(network): evaluate turn_within expectations on workflow and discussion channels&quot;">​</a></h3><p>ag2ai/ag2 · 2026-11-22T10:54:51Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged and shipped in 1.3.4. turn_within is evaluated from handoff envelopes with per-turn dedup; violations remain audited without a registered handler. No built-in hide handler: Discussion hide violations can remain audit-only without closing.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/pull/3703" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o17-·-fix-acp-make-acpconfig-a-modelconfig" tabindex="-1">O17 · fix(acp): make ACPConfig a ModelConfig <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-·-fix-acp-make-acpconfig-a-modelconfig" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 · fix(acp): make ACPConfig a ModelConfig&quot;">​</a></h3><p>ag2ai/ag2 · 2026-11-22T16:40:45Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged and shipped in 1.3.4. ACPConfig satisfies ModelConfig, permits backend-selected model=None and returns explicit unsupported FilesAPI errors. Consumers assuming model is always str get type errors; this does not change runtime permission semantics.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/pull/3710" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o18-·-fix-automations-settle-a-run-answered-in-a-shared-turn-when-that-turn-ends" tabindex="-1">O18 · fix(automations): settle a run answered in a shared turn when that turn ends <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-·-fix-automations-settle-a-run-answered-in-a-shared-turn-when-that-turn-ends" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 · fix(automations): settle a run answered in a shared turn when that turn ends&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-23T00:26:29Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Persist answeredInTurn receipts and wait for the actual joined turn before settling automation. Failed/stopped turns fail with Rerun; another message&#39;s answer is not this task&#39;s answer. Old journals without the receipt keep prior behavior.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47152" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o19-·-fix-orchestration-surface-the-paired-server-s-delivery-hold-on-send-on-receipts" tabindex="-1">O19 · fix(orchestration): surface the paired server&#39;s delivery hold on send --on receipts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-·-fix-orchestration-surface-the-paired-server-s-delivery-hold-on-send-on-receipts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 · fix(orchestration): surface the paired server&#39;s delivery hold on send --on receipts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-22T13:34:18Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Propagate recipient_delivery_held from paired hosts into send/reply receipts when recipients cannot be notified. Queued is not delivered, consumed or accepted.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/46955" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o20-·-feat-orchestration-let-agents-on-a-paired-server-message-agents-on-this-computer" tabindex="-1">O20 · feat(orchestration): let agents on a paired server message agents on this computer <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-·-feat-orchestration-let-agents-on-a-paired-server-message-agents-on-this-computer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 · feat(orchestration): let agents on a paired server message agents on this computer&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-22T20:19:27Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Final activation of the four-part implementation is merged; the first three parts alone were inert. Capability negotiation, Allow once/Always allow/Deny, request IDs and unpair settlement define boundaries; local security validation remains undone.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/46842" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o21-·-agent-conversations-route-by-where-a-request-was-made-not-who-asked" tabindex="-1">O21 · Agent conversations: route by where a request was made, not who asked <a class="header-anchor" href="#o21-·-agent-conversations-route-by-where-a-request-was-made-not-who-asked" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O21 · Agent conversations: route by where a request was made, not who asked&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-22T22:45:57Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Route replies to originating Slack threads/PRs/chats and show other work to every turn to reduce duplicate dispatch. Broader visibility raises a cross-user isolation question without proving leakage or sufficient isolation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/46759" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o22-·-fix-orchestration-resume-terminal-workers-a-reboot-or-terminal-daemon-crash-took-under-resume-work-on-restart" tabindex="-1">O22 · fix(orchestration): resume terminal workers a reboot or terminal daemon crash took, under Resume work on restart <a class="header-anchor" href="#o22-·-fix-orchestration-resume-terminal-workers-a-reboot-or-terminal-daemon-crash-took-under-resume-work-on-restart" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O22 · fix(orchestration): resume terminal workers a reboot or terminal daemon crash took, under Resume work on restart&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-22T19:51:00Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. With Resume work on restart enabled, retain Dispatch, resume the conversation and replace old terminal resources to avoid duplicate surfaces. Daemon and whole-machine restart paths differ; not locally tested.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/46643" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o23-·-fix-orchestration-say-why-a-worker-s-brief-went-unsubmitted-and-never-press-enter-into-a-dialog" tabindex="-1">O23 · fix(orchestration): say why a worker&#39;s brief went unsubmitted, and never press Enter into a dialog <a class="header-anchor" href="#o23-·-fix-orchestration-say-why-a-worker-s-brief-went-unsubmitted-and-never-press-enter-into-a-dialog" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O23 · fix(orchestration): say why a worker&#39;s brief went unsubmitted, and never press Enter into a dialog&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-22T21:58:45Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Distinguish lost Enter, dialog interception and unobserved start when a typed brief never starts; do not press Enter into dialogs. These are dispatch/start facts, not completion proof.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47087" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o24-·-fix-agent-status-redact-credentials-in-background-task-commands" tabindex="-1">O24 · fix(agent-status): redact credentials in background task commands <a class="header-anchor" href="#o24-·-fix-agent-status-redact-credentials-in-background-task-commands" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O24 · fix(agent-status): redact credentials in background task commands&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-23T00:07:35Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Redact both backgroundCommands producers before truncation, preventing recognized credentials in CLI status and worker_presence. Pattern matching is not proof that all secret encodings are detected.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47197" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o25-·-fix-doc-preview-preview-ssh-host-files-only-through-the-host-s-orca-server" tabindex="-1">O25 · fix(doc-preview): preview SSH host files only through the host&#39;s Orca server <a class="header-anchor" href="#o25-·-fix-doc-preview-preview-ssh-host-files-only-through-the-host-s-orca-server" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O25 · fix(doc-preview): preview SSH host files only through the host&#39;s Orca server&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-23T00:06:36Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Remove obsolete direct-SSH preview fallback; use the host&#39;s Orca server and fail clearly when absent. Correct routing does not establish credential isolation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47204" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o26-·-bound-mobile-reconnects-and-slow-retries-to-offline-tailscale-hosts" tabindex="-1">O26 · Bound mobile reconnects and slow retries to offline Tailscale hosts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o26-·-bound-mobile-reconnects-and-slow-retries-to-offline-tailscale-hosts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O26 · Bound mobile reconnects and slow retries to offline Tailscale hosts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-23T01:11:13Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main. Bound network-burst quick retries and slow passive reconnects to offline unauthenticated Tailscale hosts, preserving foreground and explicit Retry budgets. No real phone/network trial.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47217" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o27-·-feat-cloud-connector-wake-worker-and-connectorhost-object-undeployed" tabindex="-1">O27 · feat(cloud): connector wake Worker and ConnectorHost object (undeployed) <a class="header-anchor" href="#o27-·-feat-cloud-connector-wake-worker-and-connectorhost-object-undeployed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O27 · feat(cloud): connector wake Worker and ConnectorHost object (undeployed)&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-22T23:07:23Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged main but explicitly undeployed and uncalled. Per-host Worker objects send content-free wake frames; desktops fetch via normal polling behind connector-wake-v1. Existing sockets can outlive token expiry; new upgrades default to refusing CN. These are adoption constraints.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/47151" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o28-·-fix-cloud-address-workspaces-a-few-at-a-time-so-one-batch-cannot-exhaust-file-descriptors" tabindex="-1">O28 · fix(cloud): address workspaces a few at a time so one batch cannot exhaust file descriptors <a class="header-anchor" href="#o28-·-fix-cloud-address-workspaces-a-few-at-a-time-so-one-batch-cannot-exhaust-file-descriptors" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O28 · fix(cloud): address workspaces a few at a time so one batch cannot exhaust file descriptors&quot;">​</a></h3><p>ParadevAI/Paradev · 2026-11-23T00:24:35Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Merged bounded cloud-workspace access batching after single-request concurrency exhausted file descriptors. Production evidence supports this transaction-specific failure; exact limits/socket counts remain inferred, not a proven persistent leak.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/10170" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o29-·-fix-relay-fail-dials-and-exchanges-at-once-when-a-connection-drops-re-land-9477" tabindex="-1">O29 · fix(relay): fail dials and exchanges at once when a connection drops (re-land #9477) <a class="header-anchor" href="#o29-·-fix-relay-fail-dials-and-exchanges-at-once-when-a-connection-drops-re-land-9477" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O29 · fix(relay): fail dials and exchanges at once when a connection drops (re-land #9477)&quot;">​</a></h3><p>ParadevAI/Paradev · 2026-11-23T01:37:02Z · <strong>MERGED</strong> · target: main</p><p>Disconnect fast-failure was reverted after local wrangler dev-proxy crashes, then re-landed with upgraded dev tooling. Relay source is unchanged; 60 upstream local trials without exit do not prove cloud deployment.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/10157" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o30-·-android交付入口变化" tabindex="-1">O30 · Android交付入口变化 <a class="header-anchor" href="#o30-·-android交付入口变化" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O30 · Android交付入口变化&quot;">​</a></h3><p>ParadevAI/Paradev · 2026-11-22T20:20:18Z · <strong>MERGED_UPSTREAM_STORE_CLAIM</strong> · target: main</p><p>Official repository replaces the Android waitlist with Google Play links, updating docs/QR. Code/announcement verified, not installed or independently store-validated. Original Superset redirects to ParadevAI/Paradev with verified repository ID 1080370450; retain original radar mapping. Source LICENSE.md is MIT; cloud terms remain separate.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/10155" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o31-·-丢失响应评分分开恢复与重试保护" tabindex="-1">O31 · 丢失响应评分分开恢复与重试保护 <a class="header-anchor" href="#o31-·-丢失响应评分分开恢复与重试保护" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O31 · 丢失响应评分分开恢复与重试保护&quot;">​</a></h3><p>zambodotdev/lost-response-test-contract · 2026-11-22T19:31:07Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>A community test contract discussed in MCP #3394 fixes A5 scoring: verify operation-key recovery digest, recomputation and deadline independently, and check external effect counts for retry protection. Both must pass; missing evidence is unproven. PRs #2/#5 remain OPEN and older bodies differ from newer comments. Not an MCP spec change, universal proxy guarantee or local test.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/zambodotdev/lost-response-test-contract/pull/3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o32-·-bots跨电脑与手机员工管理发行" tabindex="-1">O32 · Bots跨电脑与手机员工管理发行 <a class="header-anchor" href="#o32-·-bots跨电脑与手机员工管理发行" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O32 · Bots跨电脑与手机员工管理发行&quot;">​</a></h3><p>stablyai/orca · 2026-11-22T20:13:44Z · <strong>RELEASED</strong></p><p>1.4.271 release claims cross-computer Bot groups, Qwen Code, phone automation/connectors/memory/skills management and WSL improvements; matching mobile build required. MIT source LICENSE verified, closing that specific prior gap; hosted/store terms and install/rollback remain unchecked. Release does not include every later merge or deploy the wake service.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/releases/tag/v1.4.271" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o33-·-bug-diskknowledgestore-read-changes-stored-cr-and-crlf-line-endings" tabindex="-1">O33 · [Bug]: DiskKnowledgeStore.read() changes stored CR and CRLF line endings <a class="header-anchor" href="#o33-·-bug-diskknowledgestore-read-changes-stored-cr-and-crlf-line-endings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O33 · [Bug]: DiskKnowledgeStore.read() changes stored CR and CRLF line endings&quot;">​</a></h3><p>ag2ai/ag2 · 2026-11-22T18:57:24Z · <strong>OPEN_ISSUE</strong></p><p>Open report says DiskKnowledgeStore.read normalizes CR/CRLF to LF while read_range retains the text. Relevant to artifact hashes, byte fidelity and backend switches. Report/script verified only, no local reproduction or confirmed fix.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/issues/3713" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="a1-·-separate-input-result-and-display-governance" tabindex="-1">A1 · Separate input, result and display governance <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-·-separate-input-result-and-display-governance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 · Separate input, result and display governance&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O1 / O2 / O3 / O4 / O5 / O24</p><p>Evidence: SDK proposals place transforms before traces/streams/storage; Orca redacts status at producers, showing UI masking is insufficient. Unverified: missing callbacks, restored object changes, children, media/log bypasses and fail-closed behavior; input changes can alter the authorized action. Carries 2026-11-19 A1/A2 and 2026-11-22 A3. Candidate: synthetic-secret negative controls across tool/stream/trace/persistence with pinned branches; unrun, no local defect claim.</p><h3 id="a2-·-distinguish-receipt-consumption-acceptance-and-completion" tabindex="-1">A2 · Distinguish receipt, consumption, acceptance and completion <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-·-distinguish-receipt-consumption-acceptance-and-completion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 · Distinguish receipt, consumption, acceptance and completion&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O5 / O6 / O12 / O18 / O19 / O23 / O31 / O33</p><p>Evidence: sharing a turn is not task completion; queueing is not delivery; recovering a digest is not retry-effect protection. November 22 local results establish per-file requeue reconstruction, not PM use, accepted artifact version or independent QA. Carries 2026-11-19 A3 and 2026-11-22 A2; next candidates are same-path version two, judge failures and lost replies. Compare task/artifact/receipt relations in FCoP, while Runtime performs I/O/retries.</p><h3 id="a3-·-separate-location-identity-and-authority-across-hosts" tabindex="-1">A3 · Separate location, identity and authority across hosts <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-·-separate-location-identity-and-authority-across-hosts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 · Separate location, identity and authority across hosts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O7 / O9 / O10 / O20 / O21 / O25 / O30 / O32</p><p>Evidence: connection reuse needs identity continuity, handoffs recheck authority, paired asks need local approval and replies return to origin. Broader work visibility may reduce duplicate work but requires cross-user tests. Request/reply/provenance contracts are FCoP comparison points; pairing, credentials and admission belong to Runtime/adapters. Paperclip remains main radar; Orca second-circle attention rises; preserve Superset&#39;s original mapping to Paradev without editing Registry.</p><h3 id="a4-·-distinguish-waiting-continuation-and-infrastructure-failure" tabindex="-1">A4 · Distinguish waiting, continuation and infrastructure failure <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-·-distinguish-waiting-continuation-and-infrastructure-failure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 · Distinguish waiting, continuation and infrastructure failure&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O8 / O11 / O12 / O13 / O14 / O15 / O16 / O22 / O26 / O27 / O28 / O29</p><p>Explicit continuation, expected-turn monitoring, restart recovery, full-disk budgets and FD concurrency affect durable work through different failure modes. Fewer conversational confirmations do not remove security gates; audit without a handler is not enforcement; merged wake code is not deployment. Carries 2026-11-19 A4/A5 and 2026-11-22 A1/A5; disconnect-history, shared-turn failure, dual-host recovery and resource-exhaustion tests remain candidates.</p><h3 id="a5-·-trial-candidates-need-concrete-adoption-boundaries" tabindex="-1">A5 · Trial candidates need concrete adoption boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-·-trial-candidates-need-concrete-adoption-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 · Trial candidates need concrete adoption boundaries&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O1 / O14 / O17 / O20 / O27 / O30 / O32</p><p>Trial candidates: pinned CodexProvider approval recovery, OpenHands Projects, Orca phone/paired asks and Paradev Android. No new installation/end-to-end local trial. Orca and Paradev source MIT licenses verified, without inferring hosted/store terms. OpenHands continuation/acceptance and mobile governance have high learning value; maturity remains untested. Costs include accounts/pairing, migration compatibility and log bypass review. Retain 2026-11-19 A7 and 2026-11-16 A2; no development assignment.</p><h3 id="a6-·-learn-how-protocol-and-benchmark-contracts-prevent-false-passes" tabindex="-1">A6 · Learn how protocol and benchmark contracts prevent false passes <a class="header-anchor" href="#a6-·-learn-how-protocol-and-benchmark-contracts-prevent-false-passes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A6 · Learn how protocol and benchmark contracts prevent false passes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O2 / O3 / O5 / O7 / O16 / O31</p><p>O31 separates recovery, external effect counts, timing and attribution rather than passing on HTTP 200 or an old digest. It is a community test contract, not MCP core. Interceptors #2624 and Trust/Sensitivity #1913 remain OPEN historical comparisons, not new standards today. Compare them with SDK transforms across layers without declaring every governance mechanism a same-layer FCoP competitor. Carries 2026-11-19 A6 and 2026-11-22 A3/A5; retain references and design negative controls, not a completed benchmark.</p><h2 id="engagement-dispositions-and-dual-source-checks" tabindex="-1">Engagement, dispositions and dual-source checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#engagement-dispositions-and-dual-source-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Engagement, dispositions and dual-source checks&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Engagement topics: how does SDK restore preserve approved actions when editors are missing? How does a failed shared turn prove an automation incomplete? How do independent effect counts prevent false A5 passes? Topics recorded only; no comments, public engagement drafts or development assignments.</p><p>Continue observing open SDK proposals and mobile governance; retain MCP scoring, AG2 expectations and older DART/SafeClaw-R papers as references, not new papers today. A1–A6 trial/experiment candidates are uninstalled/unrun. Paperclip stays high-learning main radar; Orca second-circle attention rises; Superset/Paradev keeps main mapping. Cross-user visibility, pairing permission, deployment scope and migration cost require testing.</p><p>Fresh main Registry has 47 researchers and 88 original/supplemental repository entries. Backfill uses per-source success baselines; dedup against the November 22 archive without redating history.</p><p>Of 264 source/type checks, 236 completed their queries, 25 remain partial and 3 inaccessible; five full pages do not close history.</p><p>TSA&#39;s three collection types remain 404. Transient disconnects/timeouts were retried; first-ten release retries remain partial. Superset identity verified as Paradev via ID 1080370450, original entry retained. A 64 MiB batch-save failure was recovered by retaining necessary fields in twelve split files. Some raw events await classification: successful queries are not complete research coverage.</p><p>Non-GitHub checks separately read Cursor/MCP updates and homepages of Yue Zhao (赵越), Maurits Kaptein, Lakshya Agrawal, Christian Schroeder de Witt, Shaokun Zhang and Haoyu Wang, checking paper dates. Cursor/MCP blog latest visible dates remain November 6/11, with no independently qualifying new announcement in this window. Zhao writing-pack changes retained as references; no matching new repository events for six governance subjects does not prove no activity elsewhere. Not exhaustive across 47 people&#39;s X, papers, Discussions, docs or commercial terms.</p><p><a href="https://cursor.com/changelog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cursor</a> · <a href="https://blog.modelcontextprotocol.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MCP Blog</a> · <a href="https://yzhao062.github.io/index.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Yue Zhao</a> · <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/2624" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MCP Interceptors OPEN</a> · <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/1913" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Trust/Sensitivity OPEN</a></p><p>First-party GitHub events independently support engineering facts; two GitHub links are not two source types. Deployment/click acceptance is recorded separately; research/runtime business state was not modified.</p>',167)])])}const g=a(o,[["render",i]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
